# catalog/lane-run-inputs.d/blocked-resolver.rw — the hub files one
# blocked-resolver run for project $p may write back from a Fly lane machine.
# The ro snapshot carries these plus blocked-resolver.ro. Format:
# docs/notes/2026-10-14-BH-6719-lane-run-inputs-manifests.md.
#
# The files a build record dir holds that the lane reads or writes. Anything
# else in a record (transcripts, worktrees) stays on the hub.
@token <record file> RESULT COMMENTED REAPED job.json ticket-meta.json plan.md review.md checks.txt reviewed-sha carried-note.md test-tamper*.txt iron-law-accepted-* .blocked-resolver-* .review-rescued .adjudicate-noverdict-paged .pruned
# The visit ledger is fleet-wide: a write-back carries only $p's row, merged
# under the lock br_visited_put takes.
@row state/blocked-resolver/.last-visited.tsv blocked-resolver-visited
state/blocked-resolver/$p/**
state/blocked-resolver/rounds/$p-*
state/blocked-resolver/.tick-budget-$p
state/blocked-resolver/.saturation-$p.tsv
state/blocked-resolver/.saturated-project-$p
state/blocked-resolver/.untouched-$p
state/blocked-resolver/unmapped/*
state/blocked-resolver/unmapped-family/*
state/blocked-resolver/handoffs/**
state/blocked-resolver/.last-visited.tsv
builds/$p-<KEY>-*/<record file>
builds/pool-$p-<KEY>-*/<record file>
builds/fly-$p-<KEY>-*/<record file>
state/build-notes/$p/*
# The push-rejected terminal comment's sentinel (BH-6821), read by fly-pool too.
state/pool/$p/*.terminal-noted
